WEBVTT

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.850
Oh, isn't that Ogiue?

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.760
Ah, hello.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.890
Want to come with me after this?

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.780
Is it all right?

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.000
It's fine.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.800
This way, please.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.480
Eh? So you wear contacts, Ogiue?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.580
Yeah, but I just started wearing them this spring.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.170
How bad is your eyesight?

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.220
Somewhere around 0.1.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:57.440
Oh... So you changed your appearance because you're going to a university in Tokyo?

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.480
That's so girly.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.600
It's not something that exaggerated.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.590
Then it would've been better if you'd done something about this hairdo of yours, too.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.210
Eh? Isn't it kind of cute?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.180
I've already changed it...

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.340
Once, I suddenly went to get an aunty perm.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.610
Hmm. Something seems odd... I guess it's your clothes.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.650
My switch is on now.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.420
Her salesperson switch.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.190
Yup, yup. I'm in "ruthless speech" mode today.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.190
Girl, stand up so that I can take a look at you.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.620
Hmm, this size doesn't fit you, does it? Isn't this for a man?

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.900
Ah... this... it's intentional.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:43.090
I know you want to hide your figure, but it looks pretty otakuish.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.880
Geez, isn't that a little rude?

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:49.950
But it's true, right?

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:55.240
Hmm... Well, she does look pretty lame since the size doesn't fit her...

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:59.640
Well, it was popular a while back to leave a bit of your arm exposed.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:05.580
Why don't you try a bit harder since you came all the way to Tokyo?

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.900
Please don't treat me as if I'm some country bumpkin.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.810
Rather than a country bumpkin, you're someone who's too self-conscious.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.080
Saki, she just doesn't follow fashion.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.000
Sorry, I was blunt.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.170
Way too blunt.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:23.920
But I act this way whenever I see people without fashion sense or exquisite taste.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:27.490
Ah.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.110
Yo!

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:29.710
I'm sorry...

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.960
This is how Saki behaves.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.320
As I was saying, those friends of yours are normal people, right?

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.140
Wasn't I just being considerate?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.370
You're lying!

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.090
Ogiue was there too!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.870
I don't want to interrupt a conversation among women!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:54.940
Ah, is that so?

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.190
But you acknowledge that you turned your eyes away after seeing me?

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:58.010
Erm...

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.880
That's called "ignoring". Ig-nor-ing.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.960
I even waved at you!

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.420
Ah, okay, okay. I ignored you. I ignored you!

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.540
Anyway, even if I replied, you'd have just yelled at me and complained about how much of a nuisance I am, right?

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.980
I wouldn't have!

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.480
Anyway, we were talking about otaku fashion!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.000
I called out to you because I thought that it might be interesting to you.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.010
No, I'd hate it!

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:16.890
Erm...

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:20.750
Anyway, everyone already knows that my boyfriend is an otaku.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.380
Along with the fact that I come in and out of the Genshiken.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.010
Don't act so conceited just because you come in and out of here.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:32.330
You, who can never become an otaku,
are just a life form from another planet.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.660
Shut up.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.830
One day, you'll break up with Kohsaka.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.580
Damn otaku, you're pissing the hell out of me!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.380
I'm from planet otaku!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.530
A representative of the planet of the otaku!

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:47.910
Hmm?

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:48.950
Eh?

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.720
Ah, your glasses...

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.430
Square frame...

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:00.520
You only noticed them now?!

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.900
They're... they're so square!

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.140
Eh? Why...?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.720
Why are you... trying to be stylish all of a sudden?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.990
Well... It's sort of for a change of mood...

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.320
But it seems that they don't suit my appearence...

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.420
Are they that bad?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.420
E-Eh? It's not like they're horrible...

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.230
How should I say it?

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.180
That laughter means they're bad, doesn't it?

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.940
I guess it really is the clothes.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.700
I was talking about it with Ogiue too.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.550
Ah... yes...

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.110
I guess you guys aren't interested in stuff like that.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.600
Weren't you told that's "otaku fashion"?

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.690
Are you okay with being told that?

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.060
You still wear it after being told that?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.170
How should I say this... I guess it's because we're not interested...

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.550
and we have no fashion sense?

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.020
We're broke too.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.350
Your defense mode is triggered so suddenly?

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.130
Does it hurt you that much?

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.860
Otaku don't like to get into fights they can't win.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:53.160
Yeah.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.150
About that...

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.190
On the flip side, do you think that fashionable people are lame?

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.140
"So we won't become fashionable."

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.120
Saying that you're hardcore otakus or that this is your way of living...

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.360
Are you just trying to feel superior by thinking in reverse?

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.090
Even if you say that to us...

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:06.880
Well...

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.340
Kohsaka buys both clothes and games, yet he's able to make ends meet.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.160
Kohsaka-kun is...

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.470
Well, his fashion sense and what's inside him are different though.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.820
But it's okay to have poor fashion sense.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.450
What's bad is if you give up and turn defiant.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:27.350
You don't have any interest in it because it's not one of your areas of expertise, right?

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.290
I think that's the biggest problem you otakus are facing.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:37.870
Ah! Th-They're so square!

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.290
<i>Why am I here...</i>

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:54.300
<i>Well, my original intent was to pick up a new jacket and a pair of trousers...</i>

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.220
<i>That's all.</i>

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.070
<i>Well, I've never stepped into such a nice shop before.</i>

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:10.200
<i>I usually limit myself to spending less than 2000 yen at some cheap shop.</i>

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.010
<i>I guess that's what she meant by
"letting your thoughts hold you back".</i>

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.620
<i>If I don't widen my choices...</i>

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.430
<i>Getting dizzy...</i>

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.240
<i>Come to think of it, I didn't even manage to look at the price...</i>

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.430
<i>Just entering it was overwhelming, too overwhelming.</i>

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.490
<i>How pathetic...</i>

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.120
<i>Restarting the battle!</i>

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.630
<i>I'll look at the price this time!</i>

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.800
<i>How lame...</i>

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.880
<i>Kasukabe-san, this is freaking expensive!</i>

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:03.120
<i>It's hopeless for me!</i>

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.130
<i>I can get a DVD box set for that...</i>

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.520
<i>Why the hell do I need to spend so much on clothes?!</i>

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.480
<i>I don't see what's wrong with getting cheap clothes if I can't afford expensive ones.</i>

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.860
<i>What's bad is if you give up and turn defiant.</i>

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.500
<i>No, I can't get confused now.</i>

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.430
<i>I don't really need something outrageous.</i>

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:24.000
<i>Something normal will do. Something normal.</i>

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.210
<i>I'll decide what top to get later. Bottom first, bottom!</i>

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.380
<i>Where are the trousers...</i>

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.800
Are you looking for something?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:32.670
Trou...!

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.620
<i>Shit, I shouldn't say trousers!</i>

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:35.900
P-P-Pants!

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.010
<i>I did it!</i>

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.050
They're on the second floor.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:42.530
T... Thanks...

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.410
<i>Ah...</i>

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:50.200
<i>Guess I'll go home.</i>

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.310
<i>I lost. Lost, lost.</i>

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:53.730
<i>I tried my best, didn't I?</i>

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.440
<i>The last time I spent so much time comparing prices was
when I went to a doujinshi shop back in junior high school.</i>

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:06.890
<i>Wait a minute, that's it!</i>

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:09.050
<i>I've been taking the wrong approach to shopping!</i>

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:11.000
<i>It's pointless to just compare prices!</i>

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.890
<i>The price of a piece of software doesn't determine how interesting it might be!</i>

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.800
<i>You should just decide based on your own judgment!</i>

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:23.450
<i>If I think "Hey, this is nice", then I should just fork out the money for it.</i>

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.770
<i>I must feel proud about the things I choose.</i>

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:29.050
<i>Be it ero-games, doujinshi, or clothes, it's all the same!</i>

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:32.410
<i>Why? Because... that's the kind of person I am!</i>

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:33.930
Hey!

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:34.420
Huh?

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.650
<i>Kasukabe-san, isn't that how things are supposed to be?</i>

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.490
Completely, completely wrong!

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:42.560
<i>I think that's what she'll say...</i>

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:06.560
Hi, Kasukabe-san...

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:07.200
Hmm..?

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.880
Erm... who is this?

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:15.120
A friend of my boyfriend.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.360
Ah, an otaku. I get it, I get it.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.410
<i>What the hell, what the hell, geez...</i>

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.140
<i>You  </i>do<i> think I'm a nuisance, don't you?</i>

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.330
<i>Isn't this exactly like what I've said before?</i>

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.410
<i>Just like what I said...</i>

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.700
A-Ah... yes...

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:29.780
Ah, how convenient.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.040
Yeah, it is.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.460
Let's part here then. Hope to see you again.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.630
Well, I should be heading home too.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.160
Er... ah... is that so?

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:41.980
They had something else to do.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:43.160
I see...

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.340
What is it? You still have something to do?

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.850
No, no. It's not like that.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:50.430
Aren't we... still fighting?

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:51.540
Huh?

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:53.680
Oh?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:56.200
You call that fighting?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:56.530
Eh?

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:02.080
And you actually said, "aren't we still fighting?"
Aren't you being too self-conscious?

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.500
You're so otakuish!

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.080
I see. I get it. I get it.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.240
Then, want to eat together?

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.710
Huh? W-Why?

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:16.900
As a form of reconciliation since, right now, I feel hungry.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:21.190
Or are you thinking something otakuish, like,
"It's odd eating with the girlfriend of a friend"?

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.110
What? You're still angry?

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:32.630
At least enjoy yourself while you eat.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:37.220
Indeed, it feels as if Kasukabe-san is a life form from another planet.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:40.130
We otaku can't understand you.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.680
That again?

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:44.130
Kohsaka doesn't even care about these kinds of things.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.870
That guy comes from yet another galaxy.

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.770
<i>What should I do when the bill comes?</i>

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:52.610
<i>Will the two of us order a plate to share before ordering another, or...</i>

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:53.870
All right!

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.320
<i>Looks like she doesn't intend to do that...</i>

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.170
Here you go, one large tuna sushi.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.100
How are your new glasses?

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:07.890
Eh?

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.210
You went out of your way to buy them.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.780
Ah, they're...

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:13.420
Didn't you buy those clothes to go along with them?

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.670
Hmm? Ah...

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.790
Well, it's time for me to buy something new...

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.920
Yellow tail and steamed abalone sushi please!

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.210
What did you buy? A shirt?

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:26.550
Yup. Bought a few.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.350
Eh. Try and wear them to the clubroom then.

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.030
Well, you'll just call them unfashionable, won't you?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.620
Of course.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.810
But aren't they better than the clothes you're wearing now,
which you bought without putting any thought into?

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:39.880
They aren't even worth commenting on.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.450
Bleh, how cruel.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:48.800
I'll give them an evaluation for the first time if they're clothes that you chose after putting some thought into it.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:51.060
"Give", eh?

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:52.820
Ah...

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.500
Want me to help you order something that you want to eat?

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:59.100
No thanks. It's a waste of money so I won't spend too much money on food.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.360
Here you go, steam abalone sushi.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:06.300
"Waste of money." This is the first time I heard you saying that phrase.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:08.940
Well, I'm from planet otaku after all.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.880
It's a waste of money to use it on anything other than otaku products.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:16.630
That again? You're pretty persistent going "otaku this" and "otaku that".

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.120
It's not as if you're really an alien, right?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.880
That doesn't sound like you at all.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.000
You hate otakus, don't you?

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:28.020
Hey, I'm dating Kohsaka.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.650
<i>That</i> Kohsaka.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.980
I'm used to otakus even though I hate them.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.070
So you do hate us.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.690
I've been trying my best lately.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.280
Eh? How?

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:41.150
For example, I don't disturb him when
he's watching anime or playing games.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.690
If you think about it from another angle,
isn't he ignoring you?

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:46.710
Shut up.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.780
But we played games together for a while the other day.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.850
Eh..? My, my...

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.980
There's this "prince" character.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.100
Prince?

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:06.270
He rolls something around to collect stuff.

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:08.780
Ah, part two came out recently.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.390
Yup.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.340
But it was easy to play and interesting, so I played for about an hour.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:14.740
Eh...?

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.070
Ah, well... well...

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:18.810
<i>That's... pretty shocking.</i>

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:24.070
Well... Kasukabe-san, I guess I don't really want you doing that.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:25.270
Huh? Why?

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:30.180
Well, I think it's okay that you're dating Kohsaka, but...

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:33.040
I want the two of you to have a hard time together.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.490
Woah, your thoughts are pretty evil.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:35.680
<i>I see...</i>

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.290
Excuse me, one snapper sushi please.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:40.160
I hate to admit it, but it's true.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:43.470
I hope that you'll always remain
as someone from another planet.

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:44.320
Eh?

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:45.400
What was that for?

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.700
Just a simple wish of mine?

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:58.410
<i>Well, the one who's having a hard time is me.</i>

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:00.830
It's hot!

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:06.180
Ah... how do I say this...

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.110
Here. Your snapper sushi.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.140
Ah.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.460
Want to sit down?

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:44.970
Eh?

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:48.020
It's okay Madarame, go ahead and sit down.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.460
It'd be unsightly if the guy sat down first, right?

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:53.360
Huh?

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.830
You said something otakuish again.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.420
Then I'll go ahead.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.480
<i>Well, there doesn't seem to be any drunkard around that might cause any trouble.</i>

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:17.970
<i>Anyway, Kasukabe-san can probably do something
herself without needing help from me.</i>

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.370
Welcome back.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:01.810
Ah!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.130
O-Oh!

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.500
I'm back.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:06.100
You went to eat sushi?

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.180
A-Ah... Yeah...

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:09.730
I want to eat some too.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.200
Didn't you say that you'll be playing that game the entire day?

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.040
You said that you wouldn't go to Shinjuku either, right?

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:14.900
That's right.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.220
Has the latest issue of Nenma-chan been released yet?

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.730
Ah, I wasn't free to take a look during the afternoon.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.850
Oh... Ah... I see.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:28.030
I'm going to Akiba this Saturday. Want me to buy it for you?

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.320
Would you?

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:30.630
Sure.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.590
Well, good bye.

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:41.110
What should we do after this?

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:42.710
Can I drop by your place for a while?

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:43.850
Sure, I'm fine with that.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:05.340
All right!

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:10.660
Eh?

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.660
It's not that bad, right?

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:15.800
18000 yen?! Just for a pair of trousers?!

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:20.070
I haven't bought any clothes that cost more than 3000 yen!

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:24.980
I think Kasukabe-san will find it okay.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:29.180
Ah, but Saki-san thinks it's okay to spend more than 100.000 yen on clothes.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:33.790
Here! I think she'll get angry and give me a good beating! That's how she'll treat me.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:37.760
It's okay, I don't really care. I just bought something I wanted.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.690
It takes an otaku to laugh at another otaku.

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:46.240
You said something good!
You said something really good!

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.320
Hi.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:50.520
She's here...

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:55.010
Oh?

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.940
Welcome, Mr. and Ms. Critic.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:02.970
Eh?

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:06.140
Isn't that nice? It suits you.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.940
All right, I won!

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:12.940
What do you mean by "won"? Aren't you exaggerating?

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.420
Well, okay.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.200
Wasn't that a bit surprising?

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:18.430
She wasn't as ruthless as we thought she might be, right?

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.970
Last time you would only say that I'm a mess.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:27.210
Well, Madarame, you're thin,
yet you have broad shoulders.

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:28.910
That's the current trend now.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:33.210
I see. Maybe I should get something too.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.650
There'll be a sale next month.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:39.420
No! We don't have the time to be doing such things!

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.640
Ah, Senpai do you...

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.930
You can't just buy anything!

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:00.650
Eh?

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:01.880
But...

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:06.700
At least change your hairstyle!!!

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.090
Oh, the "Exclusive for Akiba" clothes?

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.690
Chin! With that, let's go!

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:33.590
W-Well they're not "exclusive"...
I-It's a bit sad...

00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:23.660
What's the cheapest meal you've eaten so far?

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:24.980
M-McDonalds.

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:27.700
I think that's pretty grand.

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:30.580
Normally, I have udon from a roadside store
or onigiri from the school cafeteria.

00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:32.490
Oh, things you can eat standalone.

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:35.980
I know people who fry soy sauce soaked tissue paper to eat.

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.240
Why's that? Is it tasty?

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:37.920
Beats me.

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:39.800
Haven't you guys cooked for yourself?
Actually cooked?

00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:40.830
N-No...

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:42.940
It's a waste of gas even to boil water...

00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:45.320
Ah, Madarame. What's the cheapest meal you've eaten so far?

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.220
Cheapest meal?

00:23:46.220 --> 00:23:46.720
Yup.

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:47.490
Nothing.

00:23:47.490 --> 00:23:47.920
Eh?

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:48.980
Nothing!
